# The reverse direction of an energy rule on a ring bond.
#
# L(a) + R(a) <-> L(a!1).R(a!1) is an energy (Arrhenius) rule, so NFsim builds
# its two directions itself. The reverse direction has "+" between its products,
# and may fire only if deleting the a-a bond leaves L and R in different
# complexes.
#
# The model holds 100 L.R pairs joined twice, through a and b (Ring), and 100
# joined once, through a (Single). The reverse direction must never fire on a
# Ring pair: Ring stays at 100 throughout. It does fire on the Single pairs,
# which settle at an equilibrium with about 10 L free.
#
# BioNetGen's network generator agrees. Given this model it produces only the
# binding and unbinding of the Single pair.
#
# NFsim built the reverse direction without recording that its products are
# separate, so it was never tested and broke ring bonds.

begin model
begin parameters
  RT     2.5774863
  phi    0.5
  Gf_LR  0
  Ea0    0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  L(a,b)
  R(a,b)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  L(a!1,b!2).R(a!1,b!2)   100
  L(a!1,b).R(a!1,b)       100
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Ring    L(a!1,b!2).R(a!1,b!2)
  Molecules  Single  L(a!1,b).R(a!1,b)
  Molecules  Lfree   L(a,b)
end observables
begin energy patterns
  L(a!1).R(a!1)  Gf_LR
end energy patterns
begin reaction rules
  L(a) + R(a) <-> L(a!1).R(a!1)   Arrhenius(phi, Ea0)
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
